// MT6003 positive-fire: macro-call argument fails to lex (Gap F).
// The `$` character has no token rule in the v0.11 lexer, so
// `lex_fragment` returns None for the argument and the macro expander
// emits `ExpandError::BadArgumentTokens { index: 0 }`. The HIR
// macros lowerer translates that to MT6003 MACRO_BODY_PARSE_FAILED.
//
// Spec ref: §20 compile-time metaprogramming, MT6003 catalog entry.
macro echo(a) => { a }
fn main() {
  echo!($)
}
